<section class="section">
  <h2 class="section-title">6. Key Findings and Policy Recommendations</h2>
  <p class="section-objective">Evidence-based interventions, ranked by data-driven priority.</p>

  <ul class="rec-list">
    <li>
      <strong>1. Prioritize geographically targeted interventions in Rangpur and Khulna</strong>
      The single largest observable disparity in this dataset is geographic. Rangpur (mean HSC {reg['district_hsc'][-1]['mean_hsc']:.2f}, {reg['excellent_by_district']['Rangpur']}% excellent, Δ = {reg['delta_by_district']['Rangpur']:+.3f}) and Khulna (mean HSC {reg['district_hsc'][-2]['mean_hsc']:.2f}, Δ = {reg['delta_by_district']['Khulna']:+.3f}) underperform Barisal by meaningful margins and show negative or flat progression. Directed funding, teacher-deployment subsidies, and curriculum audits should concentrate in these divisions rather than being distributed evenly.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>2. Investigate the SSC-to-HSC performance drop</strong>
      Mean GPA falls from {a['gpa_stats']['SSC_Result']['mean']:.2f} (SSC) to {a['gpa_stats']['HSC_Result']['mean']:.2f} (HSC) — a {a['avg_delta_ssc_hsc']:+.3f} system-wide decline. Almost half ({a['declining_pct']}%) of students regressed from their Previous GPA by the time of HSC. This warrants a review of HSC curriculum difficulty, transition support, and student motivation between the two stages.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>3. Reframe equity policy: socio-economic gaps may already be closing at HSC</strong>
      Income quartile, parent education, internet access, and private tuition each show Cohen's d below 0.1 against HSC Result. If this replicates in official data, Bangladesh's HSC pipeline is meeting a core equity goal — but at the cost of masking where disparities still exist (likely upstream, in SSC enrollment and dropout). Redirect equity metrics to pre-HSC retention and access.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>4. Stop using raw attendance as a performance proxy</strong>
      The attendance–HSC correlation is {k['attendance_corr']} — statistically no signal. Resources spent on attendance compliance should be redirected toward instructional quality. Consider replacing attendance with engagement metrics (homework completion, in-class participation) in school performance dashboards.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>5. Audit private tuition effectiveness</strong>
      With over half the cohort ({s['tuition_hsc'][1]['count']} students, {s['tuition_hsc'][1]['count']/10:.1f}%) receiving private tuition but showing only a {s['tuition_hsc'][1]['mean_hsc']-s['tuition_hsc'][0]['mean_hsc']:+.3f} GPA advantage, the household expenditure on tuition may not be delivering commensurate value. A targeted study comparing tuition quality across providers is recommended before scaling any public tuition-voucher program.
    </li>
    <li>
